Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Removes the Windows built-in clamp on SetDeviceGammaRamp, which otherwise
; silently rejects any gamma ramp that deviates more than about half-scale
; from linear. Without this, Starlight Filter cannot shift the display
; cooler than roughly 3700 K (Gacrux) — anything below (Proxima, Betelgeuse-
; like temperatures) is silently ignored by the display driver.
;
; f.lux, Redshift, and Iris all hit this same limit; this key is their
; standard workaround. Requires a sign-out / sign-in (or reboot) to apply.
;
; To revert: delete the GdiIcmGammaRange value under the ICM key.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\ICM]
"GdiIcmGammaRange"=dword:00000100
